  ## Step 1: Identify the Big Problem
  ### Main Problem
  The school canteen has difficulty managing the queue because many students arrive at the same time, causing long waiting times and making it difficult to serve students efficiently.#

## Step 2: Identify the Sub-Problems

1. Students have difficulty knowing which line they should join.
2. Too many students may arrive at the canteen at the same time.
3. Canteen staff may have difficulty organizing and serving students efficiently.
4. Students may spend too much time waiting in the queue.

## Step 3: Apply Computational Thinking Skills

| Sub-Problem | CT Skill | Proposed Solution |
|---|---|---|
| Students have difficulty knowing which line they should join. | Abstraction | Provide a simple queue system that clearly shows where students should line up. |
| Too many students may arrive at the canteen at the same time. | Pattern Recognition | Identify busy periods and use the queue system to manage the expected number of students. |
| Canteen staff may have difficulty organizing and serving students efficiently. | Decomposition | Divide the canteen process into smaller tasks such as ordering, payment, and food collection. |
| Students may spend too much time waiting in the queue. | Algorithm Design | Create a clear sequence for students to follow from joining the queue to receiving their food. |
